{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962055-do-garous-soak-silver-damage","id":962055,"title":"Do garous soak silver damage?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-01T21:15:25-07:00","id":962055,"title":"Do garous soak silver damage?","content":"im derping here, cant remember. please help","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T21:55:01-07:00","id":962075,"title":"","content":"Unless they have a gift, Fetish, or the 7 Or 9 point merit, no they can't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T22:30:41-07:00","id":962095,"title":"","content":"Actually... it's hard to remember because it's kind of complicated.<br /> <br /> The soak rules vary by breed:<br /> <br /> Homids and Lupus in their breed forms treat silver as normal damage for the weapon in question, soaking it if they could soak that damage in that form (which doesn't really add up to much).<br /> <br /> Metis don't have this benefit.<br /> <br /> Then apply <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11674_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11674\" data-vbnamecard=\"11674\">garhkal</a> post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T12:11:22-07:00","id":962430,"title":"","content":"Quibble on merit cost: depending on the edition, it's either a 5 or 7 pointer, or just a 7 pointer. Werewolf didn't go in for Mage Revised's &quot;up to ten points in value&quot; expansion of merits and flaws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T14:36:41-07:00","id":962503,"title":"","content":"Maybe i was thinking of someone's HR'ed version which upped it to 7pt for soaking it but still agg, and 9pt for its no longer agg..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"a